      "title": "Democrats rally behind progressive Aisha Wahab after win in California special election – US politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/aug/21/democrats-progressive-election-politics-live",
      "description": "<p>First Muslim woman and Afghan American elected to California legislature held lead throughout race over main opponent Melissa Hernandez</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the US Breaking News email</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Donald Trump</strong> is in Myrtle Beach, South Carolina and set to deliver some remarks in support of Republican fill-in senator <strong>Darline Graham</strong>.</p><p>Earlier this week, the sister of the late <strong>Lindsey Graham</strong> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/19/darline-graham-debate-national-security\">said during a debate </a>that she was “not that informed on national security” – a statement that she repeated even as gasps and boos rolled through the venue.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/aug/21/democrats-progressive-election-politics-live\">Continue reading...</a>",
